      {
        "id": "lem-cyclotomic-hecke-intertwiners-and-local-power-series",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Intertwining elements and the local power-series calculus in a cyclotomic Hecke block",
        "deps": [
          "def-affine-and-cyclotomic-type-a-hecke-algebras",
          "def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks"
        ],
        "statement": "Let $H^\\Lambda_\\alpha$ be a nonzero block as in [[def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks]]. (i) Set $y_r:=\\sum_{i\\in I_\\alpha}(x_r-i_r)e(i)$ in the degenerate case and $y_r:=\\sum_{i\\in I_\\alpha}(1-q^{-i_r}X_r)e(i)$ in the nondegenerate case ($1\\le r\\le d$). Then $y_1,\\dots,y_d$ are commuting nilpotent elements of $H^\\Lambda_\\alpha$; consequently every rational expression displayed below, expanded as a power series in the nilpotent $y$'s, is a finite and well-defined element of $H^\\Lambda_\\alpha$. (ii) The power series $p_r(i):=1$ if $i_r=i_{r+1}$ and $p_r(i):=(i_r-i_{r+1}+y_r-y_{r+1})^{-1}$ otherwise (degenerate case), resp. $P_r(i):=1$ if $i_r=i_{r+1}$ and $P_r(i):=(1-q)(1-y_r(i)y_{r+1}(i)^{-1})^{-1}$ with $y_r(i):=q^{i_r}(1-y_r)$ otherwise (nondegenerate case), satisfy (3.23)-(3.25) resp. (4.24)-(4.26), (4.28)-(4.30) and (4.32); and the intertwining elements $\\varphi_r:=\\sum_i(s_r+p_r(i))e(i)$, resp. $\\Phi_r:=\\sum_i(T_r+P_r(i))e(i)$, satisfy all identities (3.14)-(3.20) of [BK Lemma 3.1], resp. (4.14)-(4.20) of [BK Lemma 4.1]. (iii) There exist invertible power series $q_r(i)\\in F[[y_r,y_{r+1}]]$ (resp. $Q_r(i)$) satisfying (3.27)-(3.29), resp. (4.33)-(4.35); the explicit candidates (3.30) resp. (4.36) do, and for them the identity (3.43) resp. (4.44) holds.",
        "strategy": "This is [BK Sections 3.2-3.3 and 4.2-4.3]. (i) On the component $e(i)$ the generator $X_r$ has generalised eigenvalue $q^{i_r}$ (resp. $x_r$ has $i_r$) by the spectral construction of [[def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks]], so $(1-q^{-i_r}X_r)$ acts nilpotently on $e(i)$ and $y_r^N=\\sum_i y_r^Ne(i)=0$ for $N\\gg0$; the $y$'s commute because the polynomial generators do. (ii) The displayed definitions are the source's (3.22)/(4.27); the identities (3.23)-(3.25), (4.24)-(4.30) and (4.32) are proven by expanding in $F[[y_r,y_{r+1}]]$ and clearing denominators, exactly as the source does (all divisions are by units). The intertwiner identities (3.14)-(3.20)/(4.14)-(4.20) are Lemma 3.1/4.1 and are verified by the same case-by-case computations, using the divided-difference convention $\\partial_r(f)=(s_rf-f)/(y_r-y_{r+1})$ of [BK (2.1)]. (iii) Verifying (3.27)-(3.29)/(4.33)-(4.35) for the displayed candidates (3.30)/(4.36) is a finite computation in $F[[y_r,y_{r+1}]]$ using (3.23)-(3.25)/(4.24)-(4.26) and (3.28)/(4.34); (3.43)/(4.44) is the source's displayed consequence of (1.14) and (3.28)/(4.34). No choice is used.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Jonathan Brundan and Alexander Kleshchev, Blocks of cyclotomic Hecke algebras and Khovanov-Lauda algebras, arXiv:0808.2032v3, Invent. Math. 178 (2009) 451-484 (complete 32-page article)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0808.2032",
              "locator": "Introduction pp. 1-5 (quiver, (1.1)-(1.4), Main Theorem (1.6)-(1.15), Corollaries 1-2); Section 2 (2.1)-(2.7), Lemmas 2.1-2.2; Sections 3.1-3.5 pp. 7-19; Sections 4.1-4.5 pp. 19-27; Section 6 pp. 29-31."
            }
          ]
        },
        "axiom_use": "None: the power-series expansions are finite because the variables are nilpotent; no choice is used.",
        "dependency_level": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-hecke-intertwiners-produce-local-klr-generators",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Hecke intertwiners produce the local KLR generators",
        "deps": [
          "def-affine-and-cyclotomic-type-a-hecke-algebras",
          "def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks",
          "def-type-a-cyclotomic-specialization-of-the-qg-klr-algebras",
          "lem-cyclotomic-hecke-intertwiners-and-local-power-series"
        ],
        "statement": "Let $H^\\Lambda_\\alpha$ be a nonzero block as above and let $y_r$ be the elements of [[lem-cyclotomic-hecke-intertwiners-and-local-power-series]]. Put $\\psi_r:=\\sum_{i\\in I_\\alpha}\\varphi_rq_r(i)^{-1}e(i)$ (degenerate case) resp. $\\psi_r:=\\sum_{i\\in I_\\alpha}\\Phi_rQ_r(i)^{-1}e(i)$ (nondegenerate case). Then the elements $\\{e(i):i\\in I_\\alpha\\}\\cup\\{y_1,\\dots,y_d\\}\\cup\\{\\psi_1,\\dots,\\psi_{d-1}\\}$ of $H^\\Lambda_\\alpha$ satisfy the relations (1.6)-(1.15) of the sign-modified cyclotomic KLR presentation. Consequently there is a unique $F$-algebra homomorphism $\\rho:R^\\Lambda_\\alpha\\to H^\\Lambda_\\alpha$ with $e(i)\\mapsto e(i)$, $y_r\\mapsto y_r$ and $\\psi_r\\mapsto\\psi_r$.",
        "strategy": "This is [BK Theorem 3.2] in the degenerate case and [BK Theorem 4.2] in the nondegenerate case, verified relation by relation. (1.6) from the cyclotomic relation and the invertibility of $(x_1-i_1)$ resp. $(1-q^{-i_1}X_1)$ off $e(i)$; (1.7)-(1.11) are immediate from the definitions and [[def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks]]; (1.12)-(1.13) from the intertwiner identities (3.17)-(3.18) resp. (4.17)-(4.18), the definitions of $p_r(i)/P_r(i)$ and the equal-colour case of (3.27)/(4.33); (1.14) from (3.19)/(4.19) together with the case distinction of (3.28)/(4.34); (1.15) is the source's five-case computation using (3.20)/(4.20) and the compatibility (3.29)/(4.35) - the two non-nilpotent cases are reduced by (3.43)/(4.44). The relations listed are exactly the presentation of $R^\\Lambda_\\alpha$ established in [[def-type-a-cyclotomic-specialization-of-the-qg-klr-algebras]], so the universal property gives the unique $\\rho$. No choice is used.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Jonathan Brundan and Alexander Kleshchev, Blocks of cyclotomic Hecke algebras and Khovanov-Lauda algebras, arXiv:0808.2032v3, Invent. Math. 178 (2009) 451-484 (complete 32-page article)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0808.2032",
              "locator": "Introduction pp. 1-5 (quiver, (1.1)-(1.4), Main Theorem (1.6)-(1.15), Corollaries 1-2); Section 2 (2.1)-(2.7), Lemmas 2.1-2.2; Sections 3.1-3.5 pp. 7-19; Sections 4.1-4.5 pp. 19-27; Section 6 pp. 29-31."
