    "items": [
      {
        "id": "ex-level-one-rank-two-cyclotomic-klr-algebra-at-e-three",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "The level-one rank-two cyclotomic KLR algebra at e=3",
        "deps": [
          "def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks",
          "def-type-a-cyclotomic-specialization-of-the-qg-klr-algebras",
          "prop-cyclotomic-hecke-algebras-of-level-one-are-finite-hecke-algebras",
          "thm-hecke-jucys-murphy-action-is-dominance-triangular"
        ],
        "statement": "Let $F$ be algebraically closed of characteristic $\\ne3$, let $q\\in F^{\\times}$ be a primitive cube root of unity (so $e=3$), $\\Lambda=\\Lambda_0$ (level one) and $d=2$. Then: (i) for $i=(i_1,i_2)\\in I^2$ the cyclotomic relation is $y_1^{\\delta_{i_1,0}}e(i)=0$; thus $y_1e(i)=0$ for the three sequences with $i_1=0$, and no degree-one relation on $y_1$ for the six sequences with $i_1\\ne0$; (ii) $\\psi_1^2e(i)$ equals $0$ if $i_1=i_2$, equals $(y_2-y_1)e(i)$ if $i_2=i_1+1$ and equals $(y_1-y_2)e(i)$ if $i_2=i_1-1$; for $e=3$ these are all cases; (iii) the nonzero blocks of $H^\\Lambda_2$ are exactly $H^\\Lambda_{\\alpha_0+\\alpha_1}$ and $H^\\Lambda_{\\alpha_0+\\alpha_2}$; both are one dimensional, with $e((0,1))\\ne0$ in the first (the block of the trivial module of $H_{F,q}(S_2)$) and $e((0,2))\\ne0$ in the second (the block of the sign module); the other four $\\alpha$-blocks of height $2$ are zero.",
        "strategy": "Enumerate $I^2=\\{0,1,2\\}^2$ and apply [[def-type-a-cyclotomic-specialization-of-the-qg-klr-algebras]]: the cyclotomic exponent is $(\\Lambda_0,\\alpha_{i_1})=\\delta_{i_1,0}$, giving (i), and the quadratic case distinction (1.14) with all adjacent pairs in the 3-cycle gives (ii). For (iii): [[lem-cyclotomic-hecke-algebra-basis-and-dimension]] gives $\\dim_FH^\\Lambda_2=\\ell^2 2!=2$, and [[prop-cyclotomic-hecke-algebras-of-level-one-are-finite-hecke-algebras]] identifies $H^\\Lambda_2$ with $H_{F,q}(S_2)\\cong F[T]/(T^2-(q-1)T-q)=F[T]/((T-q)(T+1))\\cong F\\times F$ (distinct roots because $q\\ne1$ and $q\\ne-1$ for a primitive cube root in characteristic $\\ne3$). Hence there are exactly two nonzero one-dimensional blocks, and their labels are computed from the polynomial generator: on the trivial module $X_1=q^0=1$ and $X_2=q^{-1}T_1X_1T_1=q^{-1}q^2=q$, giving residue sequence $(0,1)$; on the sign module $X_1=1$ and $X_2=q^{-1}(-1)^2=q^{-1}=q^2$, giving $(0,2)$ - equivalently the q-contents of the standard tableaux of $(2)$ and $(1,1)$ ([[thm-hecke-jucys-murphy-action-is-dominance-triangular]]). Every nonzero block contains at least one such idempotent, so the remaining four are zero. No choice is used.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Jonathan Brundan and Alexander Kleshchev, Blocks of cyclotomic Hecke algebras and Khovanov-Lauda algebras, arXiv:0808.2032v3, Invent. Math. 178 (2009) 451-484 (complete 32-page article)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0808.2032",
              "locator": "Introduction pp. 1-5 (quiver, (1.1)-(1.4), Main Theorem (1.6)-(1.15), Corollaries 1-2); Section 2 (2.1)-(2.7), Lemmas 2.1-2.2; Sections 3.1-3.5 pp. 7-19; Sections 4.1-4.5 pp. 19-27; Section 6 pp. 29-31."
