      {
        "id": "ex-degenerate-level-one-hecke-klr-map-for-s3",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "The degenerate level-one Hecke-KLR map for S_3",
        "deps": [
          "def-affine-and-cyclotomic-type-a-hecke-algebras",
          "prop-cyclotomic-hecke-algebras-of-level-one-are-finite-hecke-algebras",
          "def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks",
          "lem-cyclotomic-hecke-intertwiners-and-local-power-series",
          "lem-hecke-intertwiners-produce-local-klr-generators",
          "thm-hecke-jucys-murphy-action-is-dominance-triangular"
        ],
        "statement": "Work over $F=\\mathbb F_3$ with $q=1$ (so $e=3$), $\\Lambda=\\Lambda_0$ (level one) and $d=3$: then $H^\\Lambda_3\\cong \\mathbb F_3S_3$ and exactly one block is nonzero, namely $\\alpha=\\alpha_0+\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2$ with $e_\\alpha=1$. The residue sequences realised by standard tableaux all have residue multiset $\\{0,1,2\\}$. The degenerate KLR generators are the elements $y_r=\\sum_i(x_r-i_r)e(i)$ with $x_r$ the Jucys-Murphy elements of $\\mathbb F_3S_3$ (so $x_1=0$, $x_2=(12)$, $x_3=(13)+(23)$), and $\\psi_r=\\sum_i\\varphi_rq_r(i)^{-1}e(i)$ with $\\varphi_r=s_r+p_r(i)$ and $p_r(i)=(i_r-i_{r+1}+y_r-y_{r+1})^{-1}$ on unequal components. In this block the mixed relations $\\psi_1y_2e(i)=y_1\\psi_1e(i)+e(i)$ for $i_1=i_2$ and $\\psi_1y_2e(i)=y_1\\psi_1e(i)$ for $i_1\\ne i_2$, and the quadratic relation $\\psi_1^2e(i)=(y_2-y_1)e(i)$ for $i_1\\to i_2$, are explicit identities in the six-dimensional algebra $\\mathbb F_3S_3$.",
        "strategy": "Identify $H^\\Lambda_3$ with $\\mathbb F_3S_3$ by [[prop-cyclotomic-hecke-algebras-of-level-one-are-finite-hecke-algebras]]; the three partitions of $3$ have residue multisets $\\{0,1,2\\}$ (contents of $(3)$, $(2,1)$, $(1,1,1)$ modulo $3$), so every standard tableau realises the single weight $\\alpha_0+\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2$; [[lem-cyclotomic-hecke-algebra-basis-and-dimension]] gives $\\dim_FH^\\Lambda_3=6$, so the block decomposition of [[def-residue-sequence-idempotents-and-cyclotomic-hecke-blocks]] has the single nonzero block $e_\\alpha=1$ (all other $e_\\beta$ vanish). Compute $e(i)$ as the spectral projections of the commuting Jucys-Murphy elements $x_r$ by the Chinese-remainder formula of the same definition (eigenvalues in $\\{0,1,2\\}$, as the q=1 case of [[thm-hecke-jucys-murphy-action-is-dominance-triangular]]); the elements $y_r$, $\\varphi_r$, $\\psi_r$ are the specialisations of [[lem-cyclotomic-hecke-intertwiners-and-local-power-series]], and the displayed mixed and quadratic relations are the $d=3$, $e=3$ instances of the general relations verified in [[lem-hecke-intertwiners-produce-local-klr-generators]]. The remaining verification is the finite matrix computation in the $6$-dimensional algebra $\\mathbb F_3S_3$, carried out on the components $e(i)$ with the explicit formulas above. No choice is used.",
        "provenance": {
