              "locator": "Introduction: Theorem A and Corollary 1.1, pp. 2-4; Section 2.2 Definition 2.2 and Remark 2.3 (cyclotomic Hecke algebras and degenerate specialization); Sections 2.5-2.6, Theorem 2.8, Definition 2.10, Remark 2.13, Theorem 2.14, Corollary 2.15, pp. 11-16; Section 4.1 Definition 4.1 (e-idempotent subrings)."
            }
          ]
        },
        "axiom_use": "None: the dimension obstruction is explicit; no choice is used.",
        "dependency_level": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "ex-homogeneous-degree-check-for-the-corrected-klr-braid-relation",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "The homogeneous degree check for the corrected KLR braid relation",
        "deps": [
          "def-type-a-cyclotomic-specialization-of-the-qg-klr-algebras",
          "def-klr-grading-and-diagrammatic-composition"
        ],
        "statement": "In the specialized cyclotomic KLR algebra of [[def-type-a-cyclotomic-specialization-of-the-qg-klr-algebras]] with the grading $\\deg e(i)=0$, $\\deg y_r=2$, $\\deg\\psi_re(i)=-a_{i_r,i_{r+1}}$, fix a triple $i=(i_r,i_{r+1},i_{r+2})$ and put $d(i):=-a_{i_ri_{r+1}}-a_{i_ri_{r+2}}-a_{i_{r+1}i_{r+2}}$ (the degree of both three-crossing words $\\psi_r\\psi_{r+1}\\psi_re(i)$ and $\\psi_{r+1}\\psi_r\\psi_{r+1}e(i)$, computed on the successive permuted colour pairs). Then both sides of (1.15) are homogeneous of degree $d(i)$ and the correction term has the same degree: it is $\\pm1$ (degree $0$) when $i_{r+2}=i_r\\to i_{r+1}$ or $i_{r+2}=i_r\\leftarrow i_{r+1}$, it is $2y_{r+1}-y_r-y_{r+2}$ (degree $2$) when $i_{r+2}=i_r\\rightleftarrows i_{r+1}$ (the $e=2$ double edge), and it is $0$ otherwise. In particular the single-edge corrected braid relations have degree $0$ and the $e=2$ double-edge corrected braid relation has degree $2$; both match the two sides.",
        "strategy": "Substitute the cyclic Cartan entries ($a_{mm}=2$, $a_{m,m\\pm1}=-1$ for $e\\ge3$, $a_{01}=a_{10}=-2$ for $e=2$) into the degree of the words: the three crossings of $\\psi_r\\psi_{r+1}\\psi_re(i)$ cross the colour pairs $(i_r,i_{r+1})$, $(i_r,i_{r+2})$, $(i_{r+1},i_{r+2})$ of the successive permuted sequences, so the degree is the displayed $d(i)$; the other braid word has the same multiset of pairs. Case check: (a) $i_{r+2}=i_r\\to i_{r+1}$: $d(i)=-(-1)-2-(-1)=0$ and the correction is $+1$; (b) $i_{r+2}=i_r\\leftarrow i_{r+1}$: $d(i)=0$ and the correction is $-1$; (c) $e=2$, $i_{r+2}=i_r\\rightleftarrows i_{r+1}$: $a_{i_ri_{r+1}}=a_{i_{r+1}i_{r+2}}=-2$, $a_{i_ri_{r+2}}=a_{00}=2$, so $d(i)=2+2-2=2$, matching the degree $2$ of $2y_{r+1}-y_r-y_{r+2}$; (d) all other cases have correction $0$. The degrees are those of [[def-klr-grading-and-diagrammatic-composition]], and the case list is the source's (1.15). No choice is used.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
